            "title": "Authorization decision: guard clauses vs early-return with accumulator",
            "description": "The same resource-authorization decision in three distinct control-flow forms: carrier A uses early-return guard clauses (pristine), carrier B re-expresses the logic using multiple early returns combined with an $allowed accumulator variable, carrier C uses the cf_if_ternary nested ternary form. All three are behaviorally identical via equivalence_test.php. The early-return variant introduces the $allowed variable which distinguishes it from the pristine pure guard chain.",
